1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,214
Tree planting now dominates political

2
00:00:02,214 --> 00:00:08,855
and popular agendas and is often presented as an easy answer to the climate crisis,

3
00:00:08,855 --> 00:00:14,610
as well as a way for business corporations to offset their carbon emissions.

4
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:20,570
But unfortunately, tree planting isn't as straightforward as some people think.

5
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:24,485
When the wrong trees are planted in the wrong place,

6
00:00:24,485 --> 00:00:26,920
it can do considerably more damage than good

7
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:30,750
failing to help either people or the environment.

8
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:36,837
Reforestation projects are currently being undertaken on a huge scale in many countries

9
00:00:36,837 --> 00:00:41,520
and it's crucial that the right trees are selected.

10
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:44,480
A mix of species should always be planted

11
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:49,095
typical of the local natural forest ecosystem

12
00:00:49,095 --> 00:00:55,660
and including rare and endangered species in order to create a rich ecosystem.

13
00:00:55,660 --> 00:01:00,590
It's important to avoid non-native species that could become invasive.

14
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:07,301
Invasive species are a significant contributor to the current global biodiversity crisis

15
00:01:07,301 --> 00:01:11,540
and are often in competition with native species

16
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:15,130
and may threaten their long-term survival.

17
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:23,101
Restoring biodiversity that will maximise carbon capture is key when reforesting an area,

18
00:01:23,101 --> 00:01:28,620
but ideally any reforestation project should have several goals.

19
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:33,990
These could include selecting trees that can contribute to wildlife conservation,

20
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:38,120
improve the availability of food for the local community

21
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:41,800
and maintain the stability of soil systems.

22
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:45,300
Meeting as many of these goals as possible

23
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:50,097
whilst doing no harm to local communities,

24
00:01:50,097 --> 00:01:52,080
native ecosystems and vulnerable species

25
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:57,840
is the sign of a highly successful tree-planting scheme.

26
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:02,826
To ensure the survival and resilience of a planted forest,

27
00:02:02,826 --> 00:02:09,308
it's vital to use tree seeds with appropriate levels of genetic diversity:

28
00:02:09,308 --> 00:02:15,790
the amount of genetic variation found within a species essential for their survival.

29
00:02:15,790 --> 00:02:23,239
Using seeds with low genetic diversity generally lowers the resilience of restored forests,

30
00:02:23,239 --> 00:02:31,260
which can make them vulnerable to disease and unable to adapt to climate change.

31
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:39,420
Choosing the right location for reforestation projects is as important as choosing the right trees.

32
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:48,870
Ultimately, the best area for planting trees would be in formerly forested areas that are in poor condition.

33
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:55,862
It's better to avoid non-forested landscapes such as natural grasslands,

34
00:02:55,862 --> 00:03:03,490
savannas or wetlands as these ecosystems already contribute greatly to capturing carbon.

35
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:06,640
It would also be advantageous to choose an area

36
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:13,120
where trees could provide other benefits, such as recreational spaces.

37
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:28,710
Reforesting areas which are currently exploited for agriculture should be avoided as this often leads to other areas being deforested.

38
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:34,470
Large-scale reforestation projects require careful planning.

39
00:03:34,470 --> 00:03:36,500
Making the right decisions about

40
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:41,860
where to plant trees depends on having the right information.

41
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:51,570
Having detailed and up-to-date maps identifying high-priority areas for intervention is essential.

42
00:03:51,570 --> 00:03:57,203
Drone technology is a useful tool in helping to prioritise

43
00:03:57,203 --> 00:04:01,710
and monitor areas of degraded forest for restoration.

44
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:06,176
In Brazil, it's being used to identify

45
00:04:06,176 --> 00:04:17,340
and quantify how parts of the Amazon are being devastated by human activities such as rearing cattle and illegal logging.

46
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:27,080
A good example of where the right trees were picked to achieve a restored forest is in NLampang Province in Northern Thailand.

47
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:39,250
A previously forested site which had been degraded through mining was reforested by a cement company together with Chiang Mai University.

48
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:43,112
After spreading 60 cm of topsoil,

49
00:04:43,112 --> 00:04:51,480
they planted 14 different native tree species which included several species of fig.

50
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,920
Figs are a keystone species

51
00:04:53,920 --> 00:05:00,040
because of the critical role they play in maintaining wildlife populations.

52
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:10,589
They are central to tropical reforestation projects as they accelerate the speed of the recovery process by attracting animals

53
00:05:10,589 --> 00:05:15,030
and birds which act as natural seed dispersers.

54
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:23,350
This helps to promote diversity through the healthy regrowth of a wide range of plant species.

55
00:05:23,350 --> 00:05:26,434
Unlike the majority of fruit trees,

56
00:05:26,434 --> 00:05:33,630
figs bear fruit all year round, providing a reliable food source for many species.

57
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:39,365
At this site, for example, after only three rainy seasons,

58
00:05:39,365 --> 00:05:41,840
monkeys started visiting to eat the fig fruits

59
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:46,820
naturally dispersing seeds through defecation.

60
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:54,292
Reforestation projects should always aim to make sure that local communities are consulted

61
00:05:54,292 --> 00:05:57,740
and involved in the decision-making process.

62
00:05:57,740 --> 00:06:04,014
The restoration of mangrove forests in Madagascar is an example of a project

63
00:06:04,014 --> 00:06:08,840
which has succeeded in creating real benefits for the community.

64
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:15,516
Destruction of the mangrove forests had a terrible impact on plant and animal life,

65
00:06:15,516 --> 00:06:18,854
and also badly affected the fishing industry,

66
00:06:18,854 --> 00:06:25,530
which was a major source of employment for local people living in coastal areas.

67
00:06:25,530 --> 00:06:31,060
The reforestation project involved hiring local people to plant

68
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:34,940
and care for the new mangrove trees.

69
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:38,797
Millions of mangrove trees have now been planted

70
00:06:38,797 --> 00:06:44,100
which has resulted in the return of a healthy aquatic ecosystem.

71
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:52,250
The mangroves also act as a defence against the increased threat of flooding caused by climate change.

72
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:56,603
What's more, the local economy is more stable

73
00:06:56,603 --> 00:07:02,890
and thousands more Madagascans are now able to send their children to school.

74
00:07:02,890 --> 00:07:04,840
One other important point to consider...
